despite originally refusing to remove  controversial footage included in its  horror hit bird box Netflix has now  changed its mind the film stars Sandra  Bullock as a single mother living in a  post-apocalyptic world where monsters  convince humans to commit suicide if  they catch sight of them the Canadian  Press confirms that the streamer will  remove from Bird box footage of the  real-life Loch Megantic rail disaster  that took place in 2013 an unnamed  spokesperson for the streaming giant  released an email statement to the  outlet that reads Netflix on the  filmmakers of bird BOTS have decided to  replace the clip we're sorry for any  pain causes a lark Megantic community  for those unaware the initial curse of  bird box includes footage from a train  crash that happened on July 6 2013 in  LAC Megantic Quebec Canada that day a  freight train loaded with crude oil  derailed from the tracks and crushed  several of the trains cars exploded and  then caught fire the accident left 47  people dead a large portion of Loch  Megantic downtown buildings completely  destroyed and most of the city's  downtown area ruined and in need of  rebuilding clips of the train tragedy  appeared within the first few minutes of  Byrd box drawing the scene in which  Malory and her sister Jessica are  watching the news on television they see  massive explosions and total devastation  racking a town footage meant in the film  to indicate that the world is  experiencing a mass epidemic of  unexplained violence people exhibiting  psychotic behavior  Netflix reportedly obtained the clips  from stock footage company pond5 where  individuals can purchase images and  clips including those from newscasts  that depict sensitive events another of  the streamers projects a sci-fi  television show travelers also  implemented lac-megantic disaster  footage which travellers production  company Peacock Alley Entertainment  stated wasn't intended to dishonor the  tragic events of 2013 a spokesperson  from pond5 also issued an apology for  the use of the footage in travellers we  deeply regret that this happened and  sincerely apologized to anyone who was  offended  especially the victims and their  families we are contacting all customers  who have purchased any related clips to  ensure they are aware of the sensitive  nature of this footage additionally  we're proactively reordering content of  this nature while continuing to improve  our guidance for usage when Netflix was  made aware of the situation as it  relates to Byrd box however the streamer  refused to  remove the footage at first a  spokesperson indicated that Netflix  would keep the clip in the movie and  would be quote looking at ways to do  things differently moving forward  many were outraged at Netflix's original  decision none more than lark Megantic  Mayor Julie Morin and Kubek culture  minister Natalie wah Morin wrote that  the use of the footage and subsequent  refusal to take it out of Bird box after  knowing all the facts showed a complete  lack of respect for the people of Locke  Megantic and those affected by the 2013  disaster she said it's hard enough for  our citizens to see these images when  they are used normally and respectfully  on the news  just imagine to have them used as  fiction as if they were invented while  singled out Netflix CEO Reed Hastings  for criticism writing that Netflix was  exhibiting a quote lack of compassion  empathy and solidarity in its decision  she also stated that the Kubik  government's found it unbelievable that  Netflix wouldn't remove the clips from  Byrd box or think that it was okay to  implement them in the first place  I think it's a huge mistake now that  Netflix has reversed its choice having  already updated the film as of the  making of this video  Morin is satisfied and willing to look  past the streamers initial refusal  she said yes there was a delay but I  think in the end was more important for  me is that we have a solution to this  situation we felt was important to  settle morin further noted that the  entertainment industry needs to reflect  on this and other situations like this  to hopefully create a new standard for  the use of stock footage in films and  television series check out one of our  newest videos right here plus even more  loop of videos but your favorite films  are coming soon subscribe to our YouTube  channel and hit the bell so you don't  miss a single one  [Music]
 

